00:15:07,980 --> 00:15:10,597
to avoid a fight like
this i didn't want to

271
00:15:10,680 --> 00:15:13,177
get You dragged into
our struggles yet here

272
00:15:13,260 --> 00:15:15,731
we are it's even worse than i ever feared.

273
00:15:18,580 --> 00:15:23,077
We must make haste but humor me for
a moment there is something i should

274
00:15:23,160 --> 00:15:27,457
have told luffy two Years ago when
we first met though it means even

275
00:15:27,540 --> 00:15:33,717
more now i owe a debt of gratitude to
the people Who stopped our long from

276
00:15:33,800 --> 00:15:38,035
running wild in the east blue he had
done more than enough harm already.

277
00:15:39,500 --> 00:15:42,477
I understand that it
was you who defeated him

278
00:15:42,560 --> 00:15:47,337
so i express a long
overdue thank you for that.

279
00:15:47,420 --> 00:15:50,257
And though it pains me i must apologize

280
00:15:50,340 --> 00:15:57,237
as well don't say it 11 years ago Our lung

281
00:15:57,320 --> 00:16:01,967
was locked away by the government and
even knowing what evils he was capable of

282
00:16:03,080 --> 00:16:04,500
I freed him.

283
00:16:05,380 --> 00:16:06,210
Oh, my God.

284
00:16:45,140 --> 00:16:48,040
But what about King
Neptune? Don't look back.

285
00:16:48,300 --> 00:16:51,317
The king's giving us a chance
to make it out of here.

286
00:16:51,400 --> 00:16:52,380
The exit!

287
00:16:53,820 --> 00:16:55,220
We made it outside!

288
00:16:55,900 --> 00:16:57,018
Activate the coral!

289
00:17:00,180 --> 00:17:02,000
That didn't go well at all.

290
00:17:02,240 --> 00:17:03,417
Few guards have skipped.

291
00:17:03,500 --> 00:17:05,697
King Neptune sacrificed himself.

292
00:17:05,780 --> 00:17:07,597
And we have nothing to show from it.

293
00:17:07,680 --> 00:17:08,657
We failed.

294
00:17:08,740 --> 00:17:09,917
Oh, quit their whining.

295
00:17:10,000 --> 00:17:12,097
We followed his orders plain and simple.

296
00:17:12,180 --> 00:17:13,037
Listen up.

297
00:17:13,120 --> 00:17:14,737
This is by no means a repeat.

298
00:17:14,820 --> 00:17:17,517
We'll save the king, take
back the Ryugu palace.

299
00:17:17,600 --> 00:17:20,177
And eradicate that
pirate scum in due time.

300
00:17:20,260 --> 00:17:21,237
But first off.

301
00:17:21,320 --> 00:17:24,732
We need to contact Prince Spook
of Oshie and his brothers.

302
00:17:24,920 --> 00:17:26,737
Find the princess as soon as you can.

303
00:17:26,820 --> 00:17:27,650
Got it?

304
00:17:27,733 --> 00:17:29,637
After that, we'll start regrouping.

305
00:17:29,720 --> 00:17:32,057
And make our way back to the palace.

306
00:17:32,140 --> 00:17:35,280
Hey, we're down the closest
to where we are now.

307
00:17:35,620 --> 00:17:36,914
Fishfurley Hills, sir.

308
00:17:37,600 --> 00:17:38,430
Look out!

309
00:17:39,220 --> 00:17:42,632
Meanwhile, in the high-class
district of Fishfurley Hills.

310
00:17:43,780 --> 00:17:44,610
Get away!

311
00:17:45,040 --> 00:17:46,360
Get in the line now.

312
00:17:46,720 --> 00:17:49,367
You'll do it if you know
what's good for you.

313
00:17:49,700 --> 00:17:50,860
I don't understand.

314
00:17:51,160 --> 00:17:53,860
What do you want from us? Stomp it. What?

315
00:17:54,080 --> 00:17:56,020
It's a test. But why?

316
00:17:57,060 --> 00:17:58,377
Do as we say.

317
00:17:58,460 --> 00:18:02,220
It won't be long before
Horde rules this country.

318
00:18:04,380 --> 00:18:06,700
Now, step on the picture.

319
00:18:07,120 --> 00:18:08,640
But you can't do that.

320
00:18:08,920 --> 00:18:10,700
Yes, you can.

321
00:18:12,640 --> 00:18:15,580
At Candy Factory Town in the Northeast.

322
00:18:18,060 --> 00:18:20,240
Come on, put your foot down.

323
00:18:21,760 --> 00:18:23,000
I can't.

324
00:18:24,380 --> 00:18:25,800
I won't do it.

325
00:18:25,920 --> 00:18:27,197
I can't tread on her image.

326
00:18:27,280 --> 00:18:28,837
I beg you to understand.

327
00:18:28,920 --> 00:18:29,940
Shut up.

328
00:18:31,100 --> 00:18:35,157
Those who will follow our orders will
be branded as human sympathizers.

329
00:18:35,240 --> 00:18:39,477
Which means you'll also
be your enemy in the

330
00:18:39,560 --> 00:18:42,240
southeast outside the
fish man culture hall?

331
00:18:47,660 --> 00:18:52,400
I'll make it easy for you step on the
pitcher or get ready to leave the island.

332
00:18:52,520 --> 00:18:53,497
It's your choice.

333
00:18:53,580 --> 00:18:54,756
That ain't happening

334
00:18:55,340 --> 00:18:56,460
Come on guys

335
00:18:57,280 --> 00:18:59,000
This guy can't be that tough!

336
00:19:08,080 --> 00:19:09,660
Just step on the pitcher.

337
00:19:10,720 --> 00:19:12,640
Anyone who doesn't wanna...

338
00:19:13,740 --> 00:19:16,140
...is gonna get sliced up real good.

339
00:19:16,640 --> 00:19:18,993
At the Marine shopping mall in the East.

340
00:19:19,140 --> 00:19:20,677
What do you mean, leave the country?

341
00:19:20,760 --> 00:19:21,780
This is our home!

342
00:19:21,940 --> 00:19:22,822
We can't leave!

343
00:19:22,960 --> 00:19:24,777
No other place on the
sea floor gets light!

344
00:19:24,860 --> 00:19:26,637
Besides, you're fishmen too.

345
00:19:26,720 --> 00:19:28,937
What makes you think
humans will accept us?

346
00:19:29,020 --> 00:19:29,850
See?

347
00:19:30,480 --> 00:19:34,117
You already know how easily
humans will discriminate

348
00:19:34,200 --> 00:19:36,788
against anything that's
different from them.

349
00:19:37,180 --> 00:19:40,040
Hey, what in the heck is
happening to you, man?

350
00:19:40,180 --> 00:19:41,239
He's being choked!

351
00:19:41,500 --> 00:19:45,560
There's no way that humans and
fishmen will ever coexist peacefully.

352
00:19:45,900 --> 00:19:48,724
Your best bet is to accept
the rule of boarding.

353
00:19:49,420 --> 00:19:53,380
Under his reign, we'll have
the power to change history.

354
00:19:55,100 --> 00:19:57,000
At Waterwheeltown in the north.

355
00:19:59,120 --> 00:20:02,400
Hey, I think it's your
turn. It'll be easy.

356
00:20:03,580 --> 00:20:04,940
I can't do it!

357
00:20:08,640 --> 00:20:10,840
You still haven't stepped on it yet?

358
00:20:11,080 --> 00:20:12,460
Then what good are you?

359
00:20:16,840 --> 00:20:19,420
Hey, aren't you... Fukaboshi?

360
00:20:24,860 --> 00:20:26,297
What is the meaning of this?

361
00:20:26,380 --> 00:20:27,380
Explain yourself!

362
00:20:28,540 --> 00:20:30,520
You scum, how dare you!

363
00:20:31,280 --> 00:20:34,515
Forcing people to tread on
the image of my late mother!

364
00:20:37,620 --> 00:20:41,797
At Coral Hill, after the departure
of Luffy and the others...

365
00:20:41,880 --> 00:20:42,720
It's too late!

366
00:20:42,860 --> 00:20:43,977
There's nothing we can do!

367
00:20:44,060 --> 00:20:46,057
You're right, we let Vanderdekin escape.

368
00:20:46,140 --> 00:20:47,100
And before that,

369
00:20:47,280 --> 00:20:51,280
we couldn't stop the Straw Hats
from kidnapping Princess Shirahoshi.

370
00:20:51,700 --> 00:20:54,437
Didn't the princess say she'd
be back home in time for dinner?

371
00:20:54,520 --> 00:20:55,350
Fool!

372
00:20:55,433 --> 00:20:57,897
They made her say that so we
wouldn't chase after them.

373
00:20:57,980 --> 00:21:01,777
There's a group from the Fishman District
that's terrorizing the entire island.

374
00:21:01,860 --> 00:21:02,690
Seriously?

375
00:21:02,773 --> 00:21:04,697
Well, did they say what's
happening over there?

376
00:21:04,780 --> 00:21:06,015
This is unbelievable.

377
00:21:06,420 --> 00:21:09,397
They said that mermaids are
being reported missing all over.

378
00:21:09,480 --> 00:21:10,617
Princess Shura Hachi.

379
00:21:10,700 --> 00:21:14,229
They wouldn't sell her to the
Celestial Dragons, would they?

380
00:21:14,760 --> 00:21:16,360
Hey, awful news.

381
00:21:16,620 --> 00:21:19,457
It looks like another mermaid
girl just went missing.

382
00:21:19,540 --> 00:21:20,952
This can't be happening.

383
00:21:21,380 --> 00:21:22,556
Form a search party!

384
00:21:25,440 --> 00:21:26,700
Got another one.

385
00:21:26,860 --> 00:21:28,684
Who knew it would be this easy?

386
00:21:28,920 --> 00:21:32,180
Even so, I've just got to
get my hands on that one.

387
00:21:32,540 --> 00:21:34,952
She's the biggest mermaid I've ever seen.

388
00:21:38,280 --> 00:21:41,380
If a human-sized mermaid
can net me 70 million,

389
00:21:41,640 --> 00:21:46,057
then a mermaid that's ten times that size
is bound to bring in an even greater haul.

390
00:21:46,140 --> 00:21:47,900
It's a mermaid motherlode.

391
00:21:49,060 --> 00:21:51,531
Any way you slice it, I'll make a fortune.

392
00:21:51,780 --> 00:21:52,640
Who are you?

393
00:21:53,300 --> 00:21:54,300
Why, hello.

394
00:21:54,940 --> 00:21:56,817
Let me introduce myself

395
00:21:56,900 --> 00:22:03,900
please

396
00:22:08,480 --> 00:22:11,057
princess do not worry Heart

397
00:22:11,140 --> 00:22:13,837
may have seized control of
the palace but King Neptune

398
00:22:13,920 --> 00:22:17,097
will not give in so easily
your father is tougher than you

399
00:22:17,180 --> 00:22:22,277
realize I do still I will help

400
00:22:22,360 --> 00:22:24,500
save the king at any cost Oh,

401
00:22:24,840 --> 00:22:27,060
well, thank you, Team Bay.

402
00:22:27,400 --> 00:22:28,812
I'll be counting on you.

403
00:22:28,940 --> 00:22:30,780
Now, please excuse me.

404
00:22:30,960 --> 00:22:33,960
I have a matter to discuss
with Luffy and his crew.

405
00:22:39,380 --> 00:22:40,420
Beautiful ladies.

406
00:22:42,060 --> 00:22:43,340
Please have some tea.

407
00:22:43,800 --> 00:22:46,337
Whatever, just leave it
over there for right now.

408
00:22:46,420 --> 00:22:48,317
Yeah, you've bothered us enough already.

409
00:22:48,400 --> 00:22:50,080
We're having a serious talk.

410
00:22:50,380 --> 00:22:53,262
You're so sexy when you're
stirred with me, Nami!

411
00:22:53,460 --> 00:22:55,560
Sanchi-Chan hasn't changed one bit.

412
00:22:55,800 --> 00:22:56,740
Mmm, good.

413
00:22:57,120 --> 00:22:58,377
Idiot, that's not for you!

414
00:22:58,460 --> 00:22:59,290
Give it back!

415
00:22:59,420 --> 00:23:00,479
All right, Jinbei.

416
00:23:00,680 --> 00:23:01,820
Let's settle this.

417
00:23:05,480 --> 00:23:07,720
Tell me, what did you mean?

418
00:23:08,640 --> 00:23:12,740
Earlier, you said you set
Arlong loose into the East Blue.

419
00:23:15,280 --> 00:23:16,110
You?

420
00:23:16,193 --> 00:23:17,023
Jinbei, wait!

421
00:23:17,620 --> 00:23:18,600
It's fine.

422
00:23:20,000 --> 00:23:22,340
I heard the same thing. What?

423
00:23:23,420 --> 00:23:24,538
Yeah, a while back,

424
00:23:24,740 --> 00:23:28,137
when Luffy and I first learned
about Jinbei of the Seven Warlords,

425
00:23:28,220 --> 00:23:31,279
Yosaku told us about the
bargain that Jinbei struck.

426
00:23:31,520 --> 00:23:32,620
He's a warlord.

427
00:23:32,820 --> 00:23:35,291
In exchange for becoming one of the Seven,

428
00:23:35,400 --> 00:23:38,812
Jinbei let a dangerous fish
man run wild in the East Blue.

429
00:23:39,440 --> 00:23:41,440
Ah, is that what he told us?

430
00:23:41,580 --> 00:23:42,698
Surprise, surprise.

431
00:23:43,020 --> 00:23:44,196
You didn't remember.

432
00:23:44,480 --> 00:23:46,421
I wonder how Yosaku is doing now.

433
00:23:47,100 --> 00:23:51,688
Two years ago, when I read about you
associating with Jinbei in the newspaper,

434
00:23:52,380 --> 00:23:55,615
However, I honestly didn't
know what to think about it.

435
00:23:56,140 --> 00:23:58,817
I thought Jinbei had been
the key figure pulling

436
00:23:58,900 --> 00:24:01,488
Arlong's strings and
telling him what to do.

437
00:24:02,380 --> 00:24:03,840
So, Jinbei,

438
00:24:04,300 --> 00:24:09,360
I'll give you a chance to defend what
happened, but choose your words wisely.

439
00:24:10,440 --> 00:24:11,320
After all,

440
00:24:11,780 --> 00:24:17,700
our very own navigator here had her entire
life ruined thanks to your buddy Arlong.

441
00:24:18,480 --> 00:24:24,640
To put it simply, whatever you did
turned her world into a living hell.

442
00:24:27,520 --> 00:24:32,060
Depending on what you have to
say, I might not forgive you.

443
00:24:37,620 --> 00:24:38,780
Careful, Hedgen!

444
00:24:38,940 --> 00:24:40,077
Don't move too much!

445
00:24:40,160 --> 00:24:41,917
Your wounds could open up again!

446
00:24:42,000 --> 00:24:42,877
But he's right!

447
00:24:42,960 --> 00:24:44,577
We caused her so much grief!

448
00:24:44,660 --> 00:24:45,900
It's horrible.

449
00:24:46,220 --> 00:24:49,632
And all the apologizing in the
world won't change a thing.

450
00:25:11,080 --> 00:25:14,577
I'm going to guide ships around
all the oceans of the world.

451
00:25:14,660 --> 00:25:15,542
It'll be great!

452
00:25:15,840 --> 00:25:19,900
And then, I can make maps of
all the furthest places I'll go.

453
00:25:20,220 --> 00:25:23,161
This map's the first step
to realizing your dream.

454
00:25:23,340 --> 00:25:25,020
Is that about right? Yep.

455
00:25:27,400 --> 00:25:30,480
Nami, Nojiko, none of
us are actually related.

456
00:25:31,120 --> 00:25:33,532
But that doesn't mean we're not a family.

457
00:25:41,360 --> 00:25:43,000
Really? Pirates!

458
00:25:43,180 --> 00:25:44,680
Pirates are coming!

459
00:25:44,840 --> 00:25:45,960
Everybody run!

460
00:25:47,880 --> 00:25:52,220
Greetings and salutations,
you pathetic little humans!

461
00:25:52,660 --> 00:25:55,160
This village is now mine! Now wait!

462
00:25:55,800 --> 00:25:56,630
Yes!

463
00:25:56,713 --> 00:25:59,180
Better yet, I'll take this whole island!

464
00:26:02,180 --> 00:26:06,880
100,000 fairies for adults,
and 50,000 for children.

465
00:26:07,400 --> 00:26:09,700
Those who cannot pay, die.

466
00:26:17,880 --> 00:26:19,020
It's okay.

467
00:26:19,780 --> 00:26:20,900
Enough, Jitsad.

468
00:26:21,020 --> 00:26:22,320
Now get ready to die.

469
00:26:26,680 --> 00:26:28,300
Nojiko! Nami!

470
00:26:31,480 --> 00:26:32,310
Love you.

471
00:26:46,880 --> 00:26:47,710
What's this?

472
00:26:48,260 --> 00:26:49,840
A map, huh? No!

473
00:26:50,340 --> 00:26:51,317
That's my map!

474
00:26:51,400 --> 00:26:53,282
I drew it and you can't have it!

475
00:26:54,140 --> 00:26:56,980
A child drew this? Look at that! Abby, no!

476
00:26:58,200 --> 00:27:00,260
I'm impressed. Good job.

477
00:27:02,360 --> 00:27:03,637
She could be useful.

478
00:27:03,720 --> 00:27:04,779
Bring her with us.

479
00:27:04,960 --> 00:27:05,790
Right.

480
00:27:06,100 --> 00:27:06,930
Stop!

481
00:27:07,013 --> 00:27:08,460
Let go of me! Stop!

482
00:27:08,760 --> 00:27:10,340
Somebody please help me!

483
00:27:11,380 --> 00:27:13,792
If humans want to eat, they have to work.

484
00:27:14,060 --> 00:27:16,531
I'll be a good girl and keep drawing maps.

485
00:27:26,060 --> 00:27:28,117
Gather up 100 million berries.

486
00:27:28,200 --> 00:27:29,376
Then bring it to me.

487
00:27:30,320 --> 00:27:32,517
Do so and I will let your village go.

488
00:27:32,600 --> 00:27:34,977
In addition to giving you your freedom.

489
00:27:35,060 --> 00:27:36,637
Get that thief.

490
00:27:36,720 --> 00:27:38,177
She's got our treasure.

491
00:27:38,260 --> 00:27:39,817
Ever see just a kid?

492
00:27:39,900 --> 00:27:41,606
I don't care, shoot her down.

493
00:27:43,780 --> 00:27:45,580
Crap, find her. Run.

494
00:27:55,700 --> 00:27:59,937
70 million only 70
million more will be free?

495
00:28:00,020 --> 00:28:03,457
Oh so you made it back after all?

496
00:28:03,540 --> 00:28:05,637
I guess you had nowhere else to go.

497
00:28:05,720 --> 00:28:10,200
In that case, welcome back, navigator.

498
00:28:27,780 --> 00:28:31,217
I'm sorry, you had a
truly horrific experience.

499
00:28:31,300 --> 00:28:33,597
That's right, and she has you to think.

500
00:28:33,680 --> 00:28:34,560
I did.

501
00:28:35,300 --> 00:28:36,660
It was a nightmare.

502
00:28:37,520 --> 00:28:41,108
Nothing will ever make me change
the way I feel about Arlong.

503
00:28:42,080 --> 00:28:46,880
That said, until two years ago,
when we made the trip to Sabo Odi,

504
00:28:47,460 --> 00:28:50,037
I had no idea that even the strongest of

505
00:28:50,120 --> 00:28:52,720
fishmen were routinely
persecuted by humans.

506
00:28:54,460 --> 00:28:59,840
When Kuma was kidnapped and we tried to
save her, I couldn't believe what I saw.

507
00:29:01,640 --> 00:29:04,597
There was Sabo Odi Park,
right in front of me.

508
00:29:04,680 --> 00:29:08,397
The spitting image of Arlong
Park before it was destroyed?

509
00:29:08,480 --> 00:29:14,777
We wanted a

510
00:29:14,860 --> 00:29:15,877
place all our own.

511
00:29:15,960 --> 00:29:19,217
I'm not saying this to
make you forgive any of us!

512
00:29:19,300 --> 00:29:20,357
But it's true.

513
00:29:20,440 --> 00:29:22,020
Oh, Nami!

514
00:29:22,680 --> 00:29:25,040
Arlong, he really hated humans.

515
00:29:25,860 --> 00:29:26,980
Too much.

516
00:29:30,120 --> 00:29:32,340
Yes, we went too far.

517
00:29:35,300 --> 00:29:37,440
But for as long as I can remember,

518
00:29:37,780 --> 00:29:42,740
we yearned for the world that the
humans lived in, above. the sea.

519
00:29:48,820 --> 00:29:53,000
Arlong, me, all of us.

520
00:30:19,460 --> 00:30:23,440
My people weren't considered anything
more than fish way back when.

521
00:30:23,960 --> 00:30:24,790
Then,

522
00:30:24,900 --> 00:30:29,665
200 years ago, the Ryugu Kingdom became
a member country of the world government.

523
00:30:30,520 --> 00:30:33,344
They established friendly
relations with humans,

524
00:30:34,000 --> 00:30:38,059
and their king was even allowed to
participate in the world's summit.

525
00:30:39,060 --> 00:30:42,700
But, despite that, humans
still had hate in their hearts.

526
00:30:43,680 --> 00:30:47,957
The beginning of the Great Pirate Era
was probably the worst time in my life.

527
00:30:48,040 --> 00:30:49,746
It was hard to be a fish man.

528
00:30:50,420 --> 00:30:52,420
I vividly remember my fear.

529
00:30:52,680 --> 00:30:55,092
Human pirates running wild on the island.

530
00:30:55,320 --> 00:30:57,379
Anywhere you went seemed dangerous.

531
00:30:57,860 --> 00:30:59,140
So much violence.

532
00:30:59,540 --> 00:31:00,599
I'll never forget.

533
00:31:04,380 --> 00:31:08,020
Our only safe place in the
world was taken over by humans.

534
00:31:10,240 --> 00:31:12,300
Then came that fateful day.

535
00:31:13,000 --> 00:31:15,706
Whitebeard arrived on
the island and saved us.

536
00:31:17,740 --> 00:31:22,460
He made his powerful presence felt,
claiming Fishman Island as his own.

537
00:31:23,920 --> 00:31:27,000
Because of him, peace
returned to our home.

538
00:31:29,260 --> 00:31:33,000
However, humans continue to
be prejudiced towards fishmen.

539
00:31:33,500 --> 00:31:37,640
All of you saw it first hand
at the Sabo Odi Archipelago.

540
00:31:38,480 --> 00:31:40,340
That's the cruel reality.

541
00:31:42,600 --> 00:31:47,960
Naturally, once someone attains power,
they tend to be resisted to change.

542
00:31:48,620 --> 00:31:52,997
Even though the government theoretically
bridged the gap between fishmen and humans,

543
00:31:53,080 --> 00:31:55,977
the worst bigots were
the people in control to

544
00:31:56,060 --> 00:31:59,157
begin with the ones who
should be leading by example

545
00:31:59,240 --> 00:32:03,357
thus the relationship
between fish man and humans

546
00:32:03,440 --> 00:32:07,097
remained the same
thankfully two individuals

547
00:32:07,180 --> 00:32:10,217
rose up on fishman island individuals who

548
00:32:10,300 --> 00:32:12,337
would help change the
course of our beleaguered

549
00:32:12,420 --> 00:32:16,237
history the first was

550
00:32:16,320 --> 00:32:19,557
queen otohime she believed

551
00:32:19,640 --> 00:32:22,405
we islanders could live
in harmony with humans.

552
00:32:22,760 --> 00:32:24,936
She was Princess Shirohoshi's mother.

553
00:32:25,960 --> 00:32:30,220
Then there was him, the legendary
hero named Fisher Tiger,

554
00:32:30,520 --> 00:32:32,500
who freed countless slaves.

555
00:32:32,680 --> 00:32:33,856
That tiger guy, huh?

556
00:32:34,220 --> 00:32:36,057
I think I've heard the name before.

557
00:32:36,140 --> 00:32:38,316
To set himself apart from the humans,

558
00:32:38,760 --> 00:32:41,300
Tiger broke an unspoken rule,

559
00:32:41,580 --> 00:32:46,360
invading the holy land of Marie Joie by
himself and freeing the slaves within.

560
00:32:48,100 --> 00:32:50,677
He would go on to form the Sun Pirates.

561
00:32:50,760 --> 00:32:55,120
Many of its members were fishmen who
were formerly slaves of the nobles.

562
00:32:56,000 --> 00:32:57,640
Sun Pirates? Indeed.

563
00:32:58,900 --> 00:33:03,460
You know them as Arlong,
Hachi, and myself.

564
00:33:05,820 --> 00:33:09,820
The three of us were part of the
very first crew of the Sun Pirates.

565
00:33:11,620 --> 00:33:15,940
But we were known as Fishman Pirates,
foes of the world government.

566
00:33:16,200 --> 00:33:17,671
That's all that they saw.

567
00:33:18,020 --> 00:33:22,380
Therefore, we made it that much
more difficult for Queen Otohime.

568
00:33:22,920 --> 00:33:26,440
Bless her heart, our existence
prevented much progress.

569
00:33:29,220 --> 00:33:33,840
Queen Otohime was trying to navigate
great hardships and improve our future.

570
00:33:34,300 --> 00:33:35,800
At the same time,

571
00:33:36,300 --> 00:33:38,617
Fisher Tiger threw his future away to save

572
00:33:38,700 --> 00:33:41,465
those of his race who
were suffering as slaves.

573
00:33:42,380 --> 00:33:44,880
No one can say who was right or wrong.

574
00:33:50,300 --> 00:33:54,653
Nevertheless, they both fought for a
better future for fishmen and humans.

575
00:33:54,820 --> 00:33:56,300
Each one is a legend.

576
00:33:57,700 --> 00:34:01,100
And both of their tales end in tragedy.
